<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abruzzo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Abruzzi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abruzzo is a region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> and the Adriatic Sea, with its capital at L'Aquila. Its mountains include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gran-sasso">Gran Sasso</a>, the highest peak of the Apennines, and the Majella. In antiquity it was home to Italic peoples such as the Vestini, Marsi, Paeligni and Marrucini, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it formed part of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abruzzo.jpg" alt="Abruzzo" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abruzzo_in_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
